            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0377" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/13a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-16T23:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 16, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Have received answers from the German Emperor, Austrian Emperor, King of Great
                    Britain and President of France to President’s, offer mediation. Your message
                    reported answer given by Foreign Office but stated that the Czar was out of the
                    city. Do you know if the President’s message has been delivered to him? You
                    might discreetly ask whether any further answer is to be expected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
